{"authoring_key":"!A || \\lfalse","file":"content/normal-modal-logic/filtrations/filtrations-def.tex","line":68,"macro":"indcase","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\" data-expression-id=\"tr054-source-macro-0001\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≡</mo><mo>⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">!A \\ident \\lfalse</annotation></semantics></math>","normalized_tex":"!A \\ident \\lfalse","offset":2853,"oracle_classification":"SOURCE_GENERATED_MATH_OUTSIDE_DELIMITED_FORMULA_LEDGER","read_as":"Case: A is the falsity constant.","record_sha256":"92f7f7ea4f9366e52563f5212946a00386b84d3c37d537499794b90791ca0c97","source_call":"\\indcase{!A}{\\lfalse}{Neither\r\n        $\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$ nor $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$.}","source_call_sha256":"109c45e08c5193c4258ab1e7efd1d2f2c4af8383c3ac29cca503d2f83d2c13f9","source_definition":"open-logic-config.sty:1312-1320; unstarred indcase emits first argument syntactically identical to second argument, then third body","source_definition_preserved":true,"source_end":2949,"source_macro_id":"tr054-source-macro-0001","source_prefix_arguments":["!A","\\lfalse"],"speech":"Case: A is the falsity constant."}
{"authoring_key":"!A || p","file":"content/normal-modal-logic/filtrations/filtrations-def.tex","line":72,"macro":"indcase","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\" data-expression-id=\"tr054-source-macro-0002\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">!A \\ident p</annotation></semantics></math>","normalized_tex":"!A \\ident p","offset":3083,"oracle_classification":"SOURCE_GENERATED_MATH_OUTSIDE_DELIMITED_FORMULA_LEDGER","read_as":"Case: A is the propositional variable p.","record_sha256":"ebcae290e98e0a8b354c282859b6382351d6d2d2d2fa43e38c99a7b6e37d6b02","source_call":"\\indcase{!A}{p}{The left-to-right direction is immediate, as\r\n      $\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$ only if $w \\in V(p)$, which implies $[w]\r\n      \\in V^*(p)$, i.e., $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$. Conversely,\r\n      suppose $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$, i.e., $[w] \\in\r\n      V^*(p)$. Then for some $v \\in V(p)$, $w \\equiv v$. Of course\r\n      then also $\\mSat{M}{p}[v]$. Since $w \\equiv v$, $w$ and $v$ make\r\n      the same !!{formula}s from~$\\Gamma$ true. Since by assumption $p\r\n      \\in \\Gamma$ and $\\mSat{M}{p}[v]$, $\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$.}","source_call_sha256":"0a9ec09a70649b233445db178cae9aab82a5ff76dc0b6cc0c48b2dc7d6cbf6d4","source_definition":"open-logic-config.sty:1312-1320; unstarred indcase emits first argument syntactically identical to second argument, then third body","source_definition_preserved":true,"source_end":3620,"source_macro_id":"tr054-source-macro-0002","source_prefix_arguments":["!A","p"],"speech":"Case: A is the propositional variable p."}
{"authoring_key":"!A || \\lnot !B","file":"content/normal-modal-logic/filtrations/filtrations-def.tex","line":81,"macro":"indcase","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\" data-expression-id=\"tr054-source-macro-0003\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≡</mo><mo>¬</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">!A \\ident \\lnot&#13;\n          !B</annotation></semantics></math>","normalized_tex":"!A \\ident \\lnot\r\n          !B","offset":3672,"oracle_classification":"SOURCE_GENERATED_MATH_OUTSIDE_DELIMITED_FORMULA_LEDGER","read_as":"Case: A is the negation of B.","record_sha256":"745230c31ae60c6d58983fa4c7695e172e18ba54ff99f492b0f337e1fd156f3e","source_call":"\\indcase{!A}{\\lnot\r\n          !B}{$\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$ iff $\\mSat/{M}{!B}[w]$. By\r\n          induction hypothesis, $\\mSat/{M}{!B}[w]$ iff\r\n          $\\mSat/{M^*}{!B}[{[w]}]$.  Finally, $\\mSat/{M^*}{!B}[{[w]}]$\r\n          iff $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$.}","source_call_sha256":"fe0298530f6a4cfbab7a86a0f46b8dffaaeb187965043b8a7fc814968bc7a503","source_definition":"open-logic-config.sty:1312-1320; unstarred indcase emits first argument syntactically identical to second argument, then third body","source_definition_preserved":true,"source_end":3929,"source_macro_id":"tr054-source-macro-0003","source_prefix_arguments":["!A","\\lnot\r\n          !B"],"speech":"Case: A is the negation of B."}
{"authoring_key":"!A || (!B \\lor !C)","file":"content/normal-modal-logic/filtrations/filtrations-def.tex","line":95,"macro":"indcase","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\" data-expression-id=\"tr054-source-macro-0004\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≡</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">!A \\ident (!B \\lor&#13;\n          !C)</annotation></semantics></math>","normalized_tex":"!A \\ident (!B \\lor\r\n          !C)","offset":4422,"oracle_classification":"SOURCE_GENERATED_MATH_OUTSIDE_DELIMITED_FORMULA_LEDGER","read_as":"Case: A is the disjunction of B and C.","record_sha256":"9b28bdc7458006a7cfbcd7f54c620700246cf08e2fe2395b0987dcb943eb280c","source_call":"\\indcase{!A}{(!B \\lor\r\n          !C)}{$\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$ iff $\\mSat{M}{!B}[w]$ or\r\n          $\\mSat{M}{!C}[w]$. By induction hypothesis, $\\mSat{M}{!B}[w]$\r\n          iff $\\mSat{M^*}{!B}[{[w]}]$, and $\\mSat{M}{!C}[w]$ iff\r\n          $\\mSat{M^*}{!C}[{[w]}]$. And $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$\r\n          iff $\\mSat{M^*}{!B}[{[w]}]$ or\r\n          $\\mSat{M^*}{!C}[{[w]}]$.}","source_call_sha256":"36e233567330bae10b0ba980a2866c1c531a15d9e847b9f7e0564a6b0a86e1bf","source_definition":"open-logic-config.sty:1312-1320; unstarred indcase emits first argument syntactically identical to second argument, then third body","source_definition_preserved":true,"source_end":4794,"source_macro_id":"tr054-source-macro-0004","source_prefix_arguments":["!A","(!B \\lor\r\n          !C)"],"speech":"Case: A is the disjunction of B and C."}
{"authoring_key":"!A || \\Box !B","file":"content/normal-modal-logic/filtrations/filtrations-def.tex","line":121,"macro":"indcase","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\" data-expression-id=\"tr054-source-macro-0005\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≡</mo><mo>□</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">!A \\ident \\Box&#13;\n          !B</annotation></semantics></math>","normalized_tex":"!A \\ident \\Box\r\n          !B","offset":5835,"oracle_classification":"SOURCE_GENERATED_MATH_OUTSIDE_DELIMITED_FORMULA_LEDGER","read_as":"Case: A is necessarily B.","record_sha256":"3b604f7e293882a1e7c31d39da27ce02c8f5cf86d49cfbabeee1242f0da11f64","source_call":"\\indcase{!A}{\\Box\r\n          !B}{Suppose $\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$; to show that\r\n          $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$, let $v$ be such that\r\n          $R^*[w][v]$. From\r\n          \\olref{defn:filtration}\\olref{defn:filtration-R2}, we have\r\n          that $\\mSat{M}{!B}[v]$, and by inductive hypothesis\r\n          $\\mSat{M^*}{!B}[{[v]}]$. Since $v$ was arbitrary,\r\n          $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$ follows.\r\n\r\n          Conversely, suppose $\\mSat{M^*}{\\indfrm}[{[w]}]$ and let $v$\r\n          be arbitrary such that $Rwv$. From\r\n          \\olref{defn:filtration}\\olref{defn:filtration-R1}, we have\r\n          $R^*[w][v]$, so that $\\mSat{M^*}{!B}[{[v]}]$; by inductive\r\n          hypothesis $\\mSat{M}{!B}[v]$, and since $v$ was arbitrary,\r\n          $\\mSat{M}{\\indfrm}[w]$.}","source_call_sha256":"82b6959aab1bba1490d81b740427afa0e5c060f7b6cf3717a44355df0f3a107d","source_definition":"open-logic-config.sty:1312-1320; unstarred indcase emits first argument syntactically identical to second argument, then third body","source_definition_preserved":true,"source_end":6612,"source_macro_id":"tr054-source-macro-0005","source_prefix_arguments":["!A","\\Box\r\n          !B"],"speech":"Case: A is necessarily B."}
